cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Shadow Node Theory v2.3.1: Scale Invariance in the Node Satellization Algorithm"
abstract: >
  Replication package for Shadow Node Theory v2.3.1 (SNT v2.3.1),
  a formal model of node satellization verified across 502 empirical cases
  in 11 domains spanning 30 orders of magnitude of temporal scale —
  from digital platform behavioral cycles (hours) to galactic merger
  timescales (billions of years). The central finding is that
  satellization dynamics follow a power law R(t) = a·t^b invariant
  to temporal scale and substrate, with institutional friction as the
  dominant predictor of the exponent b. Includes code for all analyses,
  data for reproducible cases, and four specialized papers targeting
  PLOS Complex Systems, Journal of Theoretical Biology, The Astrophysical
  Journal, and Investigación Económica.
